cmd_help() {
cat <<EOF
mirage — Kafka Connect incident trainer (KCD / Strimzi)

  ${C_B}setup${C_0}              create cluster + Strimzi + Kafka + Connect + ingress
  ${C_B}list${C_0}               list labs and your results
  ${C_B}start <n>${C_0}          inject lab n's fault(s)
  ${C_B}stop [n]${C_0}           grade your fix (defaults to the active lab)
  ${C_B}hint [n] [level]${C_0}   a nudge, one step at a time (run again for more)
  ${C_B}solve [n]${C_0}          the full answer
  ${C_B}why [n]${C_0}            debrief: the mechanism, the signal, the rule
  ${C_B}answer <n> <v>${C_0}     record a triage conclusion (e.g. answer 8 broker)
  ${C_B}next${C_0}               show the next lab in the recommended order

  ${C_B}status${C_0}             cluster + lab overview
  ${C_B}verify${C_0}             health-check the whole environment end to end
  ${C_B}counts${C_0}             source vs target counts, plus a live replication delta
  ${C_B}diff${C_0}               baseline vs running state, and CR vs worker runtime
  ${C_B}intro${C_0}              how the labs work — read this first
  ${C_B}env${C_0}                print the KUBECONFIG line for raw kubectl
  ${C_B}api [path]${C_0}         Connect REST API through the ingress (e.g. api /connectors)
  ${C_B}kafka [side]${C_0}       expose a broker on localhost:9092 for your own kafka-* CLI
                     ${C_DIM}source (default) | target | stop | status${C_0}
  ${C_B}kcli <side> <tool>${C_0} run a Kafka CLI tool against either cluster, no forward
                     ${C_DIM}e.g. kcli target topics --list${C_0}
  ${C_B}topics${C_0}             topics on both clusters
  ${C_B}logs [lines]${C_0}       tail a Connect worker
  ${C_B}logs --errors${C_0}      only known failure signatures, with what they mean
  ${C_B}metrics [pattern]${C_0}  scrape the JMX exporter on :9404

  ${C_B}reset [--fresh]${C_0}     restore the baseline; --fresh also empties the topic
  ${C_B}repair${C_0}             rebuild the Connect cluster when the environment is wedged
  ${C_B}teardown${C_0}           delete the cluster

Cluster provider: kind by default, minikube also supported.
